{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfy43VJqZppNxcd2draDo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## The rule\n\n`docs/behavior/returns/submit-return.md:10` (`{#partial-refund}`) states it:\n\n> The refund is the price paid for the returned items, with the order's discount applied and rounded half up to the cent\n\nSo: sum the returned items at their order-time unit price, apply the order's discount percentage, round half up.\n\n## The code\n\n`calculateRefund` in `src/returns.ts:18-25`:\n\n```ts\nconst subtotal = items.reduce((sum, item) => {\n  const line = order.lines.find((l) => l.productId === item.productId);\n  if (!line) throw new Error(`Product ${item.productId} is not on order ${order.id}`);\n  return sum + line.unitPriceCents * item.quantity;   // returned items only\n}, 0);\nreturn Math.round(subtotal * (1 - order.discountPercent / 100));   // discount + rounding\n```\n\nThree things worth noting about *which* numbers it uses:\n\n- **`line.unitPriceCents`, not the catalogue price.** Price is snapshotted onto the order at `createOrder` time (`src/orders.ts:33`), so a later price change in `src/products.ts` can't move an old refund.\n- **Only the returned lines.** The untouched items on the order never enter the subtotal — that's what makes it a *partial* refund.\n- **Discount and rounding apply once, to the whole returned subtotal** — not per item.\n\n`submitReturn` calls it at `src/returns.ts:50` and stores the result as `refundCents` at request time; `approveReturn` and `refundReturn` only move `status` and never recompute, so the amount is frozen when the return is requested.\n\n## But the code doesn't match the rule\n\nThe spec's own worked example fails. A trail map (850) at 33% off should refund 570:\n\n```\nspec says refund      : 570\ncalculateRefund gives : 569\norderTotalCents gives : 570   (same money, same discount, different code path)\n```\n\nThe exact value is 569.5, which half-up rounds to 570. `Math.round` *is* half-up — the problem is that it never sees 569.5. `1 - 33/100` is `0.6699999999999999` in binary floating point, so `850 * 0.6699999999999999` is `569.4999999999999`, which rounds down. The customer loses a cent.\n\n`orderTotalCents` (`src/orders.ts:43-47`) already avoids this by staying in integers — `Math.floor((subtotal * (100 - discountPercent) + 50) / 100)` — with a comment saying exactly that. `calculateRefund` was written the other way, so the two paths disagree on the same money.\n\nIt affects any tie: 33% off a 150 subtotal gives 100 instead of 101, and 33% off 2550 gives 1708 instead of 1709.\n\n```\n★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────\n• The bug is in the *expression shape*, not the rounding function. `x * (1 - d/100)` builds an inexact multiplier first; `x * (100 - d) / 100` keeps every intermediate an exact integer. Same algebra, different floating-point outcome.\n• The existing suite can't catch it: `test/returns.test.ts` asserts 1990 (no discount) and 1800 (10% off 2000) — both land on exact cents, so no tie is ever exercised. The orders tests *do* cover a tie (1692, at `test/orders.test.ts:25`), which is why the integer path there is correct and commented.\n• Rounding once on the summed subtotal also makes refunds non-additive: two trail maps in one return refunds 1139, but returned one at a time it's 569 + 569 = 1138. Worth deciding deliberately, since support can split a return.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n```\n\nAll 14 tests currently pass — the defect is invisible to them.\n\nPer `AGENTS.md`, a fix belongs to a spec in `docs/specs/`, and there are none yet. Want me to run `spec-start` for a returns-rounding spec, align `calculateRefund` with the integer approach in `orders.ts`, and add the tie cases (including the spec's own 8.50-at-33% example) as tests? I'd also want a decision from you on the non-additive rounding before touching that part."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":963,"cache_read_input_tokens":77747,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":963},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e1e3083-cac6-4305-85b9-1f4a5ca8823b","uuid":"e12558d6-9024-4094-8723-94a66fb15edf","timestamp":"2026-10-12T21:28:57.673Z","request_id":"req_011Cfy43V6SABC8yuXSq4xdz"}
